// CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// Step-by-step math CSD with delimiter-triggered constrained spans. The strategy
// tracks the usual generation state plus an `activeGroups` view of the caller-
// supplied `validTokenGroups`. Outside `<< >>`, it generates freely until EOS
// or an opening delimiter token `<<` appears. Inside a constrained span, it
// uses the parser-valid prefix `currentConstrainedOut` as the main state and
// chooses between two constrained samplers: an adaptive group-boosted sampler
// when caller groups are available, and a plain constrained step otherwise.
//
// The main observation is that for this task, arithmetic work should happen
// inside `<< >>`, so validity is enforced only there. The parser-valid prefix
// tracks the in-progress arithmetic expression, and completion detection
// (`parser.IsCompletePrefix`) decides when the span can be closed with `>>`.
// Group boosts are a soft preference only; the hard parser mask still ensures
// every non-EOS token appended inside the span keeps the arithmetic fragment
// valid.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity: In the unconstrained branch, entering a span happens only
//   when next == "<<"; we then set currentConstrainedOut := [], and the method
//   precondition gives parser.IsValidPrefix([]). In the close branch,
//   CloseConstrainedSpan sets insideConstrainedOut to false, so the implication
//   becomes vacuous. In the constrained branches, AdaptiveConstrainedStep and
//   ConstrainedStep both return either EOS or a token that is parser-valid next;
//   on the non-EOS path, AppendConstrainedToken preserves parser validity.
//
// suffix: In the unconstrained branch, if we stay outside then the implication
//   is vacuous; if we enter a span, currentConstrainedOut is [] so the length-0
//   suffix of generated matches it. In the close branch, CloseConstrainedSpan
//   appends the closing delimiter and resets currentConstrainedOut to [], so
//   the implication is again vacuous. In each constrained append branch, the
//   same token is appended to both generated and currentConstrainedOut via
//   AppendConstrainedToken, so the suffix equality is preserved.
//
// cost accounting: We return cost := steps, so it suffices to maintain
//   0 <= steps <= maxSteps. Every non-breaking branch increments steps by 1:
//   UnconstrainedStep, CloseConstrainedSpan, AdaptiveConstrainedStep, and
//   ConstrainedStep are all cost-bumping single-step helpers. Breaking branches
//   also occur only after such a helper call in that iteration, so steps still
//   reflects the work done and remains within maxSteps.
//
// progress bound: In the unconstrained branch, either EOS breaks immediately or
//   exactly one token is appended and steps := steps + 1, preserving
//   |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps. In the close branch, at most one
//   delimiter token is appended while steps increases by 1. In each constrained
//   branch, EOS causes no append and breaks, or one valid token is appended via
//   AppendConstrainedToken while steps increases by 1; hence the linear bound
//   on generated length is preserved in every non-breaking branch.
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END
generated := generatedPrefix;
insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;
currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;
cost := 0;

var steps: nat := 0;
var activeGroups := validTokenGroups;

while steps < maxSteps
